  "details": "Description\n\nSince build 1358, while using Fixed Foveated Rendering, VRChat seems to freeze when certain objects are in view. This was not the case in builds prior to 1358.\n\nMy guess is that this particular object includes not only world objects, but also some avatars; even in worlds where I visited alone and had no problems, this bug occurred when I was with several players. Note that this did not seem to be caused by shaders or animations, as it occurred even when all shaders and animations of the avatar were turned off using safety.\n\nI have listed one world where the phenomenon occurs in the reproduction procedure below, but we have confirmed that the bug occurs in other worlds as well.\n\nP.S. This bug did not occur in open beta Build 1370.\n\n--------------------\n\nReproduction steps\n\n1. Go to the world in the link below. (https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_f4754514-4f72-4cad-b428-a5b0f13fb8c0)\n\n2. Enable Fixed Foveated Rendering.\n\n3. Look around near the respawn point.",
